# The corpus and the vendored upstream suites are byte-exact copies of published
# artifacts, and their sha256 digests are recorded in dataset/00_raw/PROVENANCE.json
# and tests/TESTS_PROVENANCE.json. Git must not normalise line endings in them:
# two corpus files ship CRLF, and rewriting those bytes on commit or checkout
# would break every digest and with it the reproducibility claim.
dataset/**       -text
tests/_upstream/** -text
